    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d649">

                <pb facs="1121" n="1061" xml:id="pg1061"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr. Sullivan.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 36.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1868-03-30"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >March</hi> 30, 1868.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> Mr. Philip B. Livingston, the commercial
                    agent of the United States at Saint Andrews, represents that that island is
                    quite destitute of any government, and that the lives and property of citizens
                    of the United States have no protection. You will inquire into and report upon
                    this subject. It is particularly desirable to know whether any national interest
                    of the United States is endangered by the condition of affairs at the island as
                    represented.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Peter</hi> J. <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Sullivan,</hi> Esq., <hi rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c.,
                            &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
